num_vec = pci_msix_vec_count(cptvf->pdev);
if (num_vec <= 0)
```
Reason:
The variable `num_vec` is declared as an unsigned integer (`u32`). If `pci_msix_vec_count(cptvf->pdev)` returns a negative value (indicating an error), it will be converted to a large positive value due to unsigned integer behavior. Consequently, the condition `if (num_vec <= 0)` will never be true, leading to improper error handling.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
int num_vec;
if (num_vec <= 0)
```
Reason:
Changing the type of `num_vec` from `u32` to `int` allows it to correctly represent negative values. This ensures that if `pci_msix_vec_count(cptvf->pdev)` returns a negative value, the condition `if (num_vec <= 0)` will evaluate to true, enabling proper error handling.

